      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/finally_available_again_l135__en/",
      "html": "<p>The L-catfish L135 is one of the most attractive L-numbers. Most specialists currently believe that it represents a variety of the species Peckoltia braueri. This species has also been given two other L-numbers, L121 and L305. L135 is the most colourful of them. It attains a maximum length of 12-15 cm and has already been bred in aquaria.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/finally_available_again_l135__en/",
      "html": "<p>It is only very rarely available as wild-collected stock.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/finally_available_again_l135__en/",
      "html": "<p>L135 comes from the central Rio Negro basin.</p>"
